// Generated by scripts/sync-checklists.mjs from HERO_CHECKLISTS.md. Do not edit by hand.
export const CHECKLISTS_TEXT = "# Hero mechanics checklists\n\nVersion: 2026-11-26\n\nThe checklists for Hero mechanics (RUBRIC.md §10), one per hero in the game. Both apps read this file: `scripts/sync-checklists.sh` copies it into the Mac app and `windows/scripts/sync-checklists.mjs` into the Windows app. Tests fail when a hero in the catalog has no checklist.\n\nHow they were written:\n- 2026-11-26, from the official ability and perk lists on Blizzard's hero pages (read through the OverFast API), so ability names match the current game.\n- An ability that isn't on the hero page is only named when a perk on that page names it (Jagged Blade, the chainguns).\n- The hero pages don't say which ability is the ultimate for the newest heroes, so those checklists don't say it either.\n- Every item describes good use that can be seen in the footage: when the ability is used, on whom, and what it's kept for.\n- Perks change how some abilities work; an item that a chosen perk replaces (for example Stim Pack instead of Biotic Field) is judged as the perk version.\n\nChange this file when a patch changes a kit, raise the version, then run both sync scripts.\n\n## Ana · `ana`\n- Biotic Rifle shots land on the ally who is taking damage, from a spot behind cover, not on allies at full health.\n- Sleep Dart is held for a diver, a flanker or a channelled enemy ultimate, not fired at a tank at the start of a fight.\n- Biotic Grenade lands on the enemy the team is focusing (no healing for them) or on several hurt allies at once, not into empty space.\n- Nano Boost goes to an ally who is in reach of enemies and can use it right away: an engage, their ultimate, or a tank under focus.\n- When a diver reaches her, she uses Sleep Dart or Biotic Grenade and moves toward cover or her team instead of trading shots.\n\n## Anran · `anran`\n- Zhuque Fans keep enemies burning (Ignition) before Fan the Flames is used, so the blast amplifies the burn.\n- Inferno Rush is used to reach a burning or isolated target, or to get out, not to rush alone into the enemy team.\n- Dancing Blaze is used when enemies shoot at her or several enemies are close, so she dodges damage and heals from each hit.\n- Vermillion Ascent is aimed into enemies standing together, so the explosion ignites several of them.\n- She fights near cover and leaves once Dancing Blaze and Inferno Rush are both used.\n\n## Ashe · `ashe`\n- Scoped shots from The Viper are aimed at heads at range; unscoped shots only at close range.\n- Dynamite lands on grouped enemies or behind a barrier and is shot to blow up at once, before she fires on the burning targets.\n- Coach Gun is used to reach high ground or to push a diver away, and is kept while an enemy flanker is alive.\n- B.O.B. is sent where the team can shoot the enemies he knocks up, or onto the objective to stall it, not into an empty area.\n- She reloads behind cover between fights, not in the middle of a duel in the open.\n\n## Baptiste · `baptiste`\n- Healing grenades from the Biotic Launcher land next to hurt allies, with bursts at enemies in between.\n- Regenerative Burst is used when he or several allies are below half health, not when everyone is full.\n- Immortality Field is thrown to save an ally who would die, or against an enemy ultimate, behind cover where it isn't destroyed at once.\n- Amplification Matrix is placed in front of allies who are shooting at enemies, during a fight.\n- Exo Boots jumps are used to reach high ground or to dodge a diver.\n\n## Bastion · `bastion`\n- Reconfigures to Configuration: Assault next to cover, with a support nearby and targets in range.\n- Configuration: Recon shots are aimed at heads at range; he doesn't stand in the open in Recon.\n- A-36 Tactical Grenade is used for burst on a target, and its knockback to escape or reach high ground.\n- Configuration: Artillery shells land on enemies who can't move (crowd control) or on grouped enemies, not on open ground.\n- He leaves Configuration: Assault before it runs out in a safe spot, not stranded in the open as it ends.\n\n## Brigitte · `brigitte`\n- Rocket Flail and Whip Shot hits keep Inspire active while she stays close enough to heal her allies.\n- Repair Pack goes to the ally taking damage, not to allies at full health.\n- Whip Shot knocks a diver or flanker away from her backline, rather than hitting a tank.\n- Barrier Shield is raised against burst on herself or a nearby ally; Shield Bash closes the gap on a flanker.\n- Rally is used when allies are close by, as the team engages or as divers arrive.\n- She stays with her backline to protect it instead of chasing enemies.\n\n## Cassidy · `cassidy`\n- Peacekeeper's primary fire is aimed at heads at mid range; the fan of remaining rounds only at close range on a target it will kill.\n- Combat Roll is used to reload mid-fight or to dodge, not to roll into the enemy team.\n- Flashbang is held for a diver or flanker at close range and followed by shots.\n- Deadeye is used from cover or while enemies are distracted, and fired once the targets are locked, not after he is already being shot.\n- He fights at mid range from cover, not at long range where Peacekeeper loses damage.\n\n## D.Mon · `dmon`\n- Power Barrier is held while the enemy shoots at the team, and lowered to deal damage when they stop.\n- Surging Strike is used from behind Power Barrier to push enemies off the objective or off high ground.\n- Propulsors' fuel is used to close the distance or to retreat, with fuel left for the way out.\n- Plasma Saber swings land on targets in reach; Fusion Repeater is used for enemies out of saber range.\n- Limit Break is used when several enemies are in front of him and the team can follow up on the amplified damage.\n- After Eject!, he backs off to safety until Call Mech is ready, instead of fighting in the open.\n\n## Doctrine · `doctrine`\n- Eternal Scepter heals the ally taking damage, and damages enemies while the team is healthy.\n- Infuse goes on the ability the moment needs: Shrouded Momentum to escape or reach high ground, Invigorating Drones when she and an ally both fight, Eternal Scepter for a piercing blast through grouped enemies.\n- Invigorating Drones go to an ally who is fighting or taking damage.\n- Shrouded Momentum is kept as an escape from divers or used to reposition, not to rush into the enemy team.\n- Deliverance is launched as the team fights, so the overhealth and the lower enemy health decide the fight.\n\n## Domina · `domina`\n- Photon Magnum's beam stays on one target at medium range until the high-impact shot lands.\n- Barrier Array is placed to cover the team's advance or to block a dangerous angle, not where nobody stands.\n- Sonic Repulsors push enemies into walls for the stun, or push divers off her allies.\n- Crystal Charge is placed on enemies or a choke and detonated while they are in it.\n- Panopticon is fired at several enemies, with the team ready to shoot them before it detonates.\n- She backs off to cover when her shields are down instead of staying in front.\n\n## Doomfist · `doomfist`\n- Rocket Punch is charged and aimed to hit a target into a wall, or used to escape, not punched into the enemy team with no way out.\n- Power Block is used against heavy damage, and the empowered Rocket Punch is then used.\n- Seismic Slam is used to engage or to reach a target, combined with Hand Cannon shots and Rocket Punch.\n- Hand Cannon shots are fired between abilities at close range.\n- Meteor Strike lands on grouped enemies to engage, or is used to escape, not on a single target.\n- He dives with his cooldowns ready and leaves once they are used, not staying in with all of them down.\n\n## D.Va · `dva`\n- Defense Matrix eats important projectiles and enemy ultimates, not used while nothing is shot at the team.\n- Boosters are used to dive the backline with the team or to protect allies, with enough left to get out.\n- Micro Missiles are fired together with Fusion Cannons for burst on a target in range.\n- Fusion Cannons are used at close range where the spread hits, not at long range.\n- Self-Destruct is placed where enemies can't escape it (around a corner, on the objective, after crowd control) or to force them off the objective.\n- After Eject!, she finds cover and uses Light Gun safely until Call Mech is ready.\n\n## Echo · `echo`\n- Sticky Bombs are fired at a target and followed with Tri-Shot at close to medium range.\n- Focusing Beam is used only on targets under half health, where it does very high damage.\n- Flight is used to take high-ground angles or to escape, then Glide to stay in the air.\n- Duplicate copies a hero whose ultimate fits the moment, and the copied ultimate is used.\n- She stays at high-ground angles out of enemy hitscan sightlines, not hovering in the open.\n\n## Emre · `emre`\n- Synthetic Burst Rifle bursts are aimed at heads, zoomed in at range and unzoomed up close.\n- Cyber Frag is bounced into grouped enemies or around corners so it explodes on a target.\n- Override Protocol is used when targets are in reach and he can stay in the fight while it lasts.\n- He breaks line of sight after taking damage so Altered Vitals' regeneration starts, instead of staying in the open.\n- He fights at mid range from an off-angle, not standing in front of his tank.\n\n## Freja · `freja`\n- Take Aim bolts are aimed at a target, and Quick Dash is used to refresh Take Aim for another shot.\n- Quick Dash and Updraft are used to reach off-angles or high ground, with one kept to escape.\n- Automatic bolts finish targets between Take Aim shots.\n- Bola Shot hits a target standing near other enemies, so it pulls them together for the team.\n- She takes duels from the air or from high ground, out of enemy hitscan sightlines.\n\n## Genji · `genji`\n- Shuriken bursts are aimed at heads at range; the fan is used at close range for burst.\n- Deflect is used against incoming projectiles or ultimates, or to cross a dangerous area, not while nobody shoots at him.\n- Swift Strike finishes low targets (an elimination resets it) or gets him out.\n- Dragonblade is used when the team engages, on targets that aren't protected.\n- Cyber-Agility (wall climb, double jump) is used to take high ground and to dodge.\n- He engages low-health or isolated targets, not the whole enemy team.\n\n## Hanzo · `hanzo`\n- Storm Bow arrows are fully charged before firing at range and aimed at heads.\n- Sonic Arrow is placed to scout a corner or a flank before a fight.\n- Storm Arrows are used at close range or to finish a target.\n- Lunge and Wall Climb are used to reach high ground and to dodge divers.\n- Dragonstrike is fired through a choke or at enemies who can't move, often after crowd control.\n\n## Hazard · `hazard`\n- Bonespur bursts are fired at close to medium range at the target the team is focusing.\n- Spike Guard is held against enemy burst, regaining ammo and firing spikes, and released before its energy runs out.\n- Violent Leap is used to engage and followed by the slash to knock enemies back, or kept as the escape when outnumbered.\n- Jagged Wall knocks enemies off the objective or off a ledge, or blocks a flank.\n- Downpour is used on grouped enemies with the team ready to hit the immobilized targets.\n- Vault is used to climb onto high ground or to escape.\n\n## Illari · `illari`\n- Solar Rifle shots are fully charged before firing at range.\n- The healing beam goes to allies taking damage, without draining all her solar energy.\n- Healing Pylon is placed behind cover where it sees the team, and placed again after it is destroyed.\n- Outburst is used to escape a diver or to reach high ground.\n- Captive Sun hits grouped enemies when the team can follow up with damage so they explode.\n\n## Jetpack Cat · `jetpack-cat`\n- Biotic Pawjectiles heal allies taking damage, and damage enemies while the team is healthy.\n- Lifeline tows an ally to high ground, to an angle or out of danger.\n- Purr is used when several allies are hurt, or when an enemy is close so its knockback pushes them away.\n- Frenetic Flight keeps her out of enemy hitscan sightlines, with fuel kept for the escape.\n- Catnapper is aimed at grouped enemies so it knocks down several of them, with the team ready to follow up.\n\n## Junker Queen · `junker-queen`\n- Scattergun is fired at close range; Jagged Blade is thrown at a target and recalled to pull it in.\n- Carnage is swung into several enemies to wound them and lower its cooldown.\n- Commanding Shout is used as the team engages or takes burst damage, so allies get the extra health.\n- Rampage wounds several enemies and stops their healing, with the team following up.\n- She keeps wounding enemies so Adrenaline Rush heals her, and stays in the fight while it does.\n\n## Junkrat · `junkrat`\n- Frag Launcher grenades are bounced into chokes and around corners; direct hits at close range.\n- Concussion Mine is used for burst (mine plus frags), or to jump away or onto high ground.\n- Steel Trap is placed on a flank route or next to himself to catch divers.\n- RIP-Tire is driven along walls or a hidden route into grouped enemies or the backline.\n- He uses Total Mayhem: frags and mine jumps at close range, since his explosives don't hurt him.\n\n## Juno · `juno`\n- Mediblaster bursts land on allies taking damage, and on enemies while the team is healthy.\n- Pulsar Torpedoes are locked onto several allies or enemies before firing.\n- Hyper Ring is placed where the team advances or retreats.\n- Glide Boost and Martian Overboots are used to escape divers and to reposition.\n- Orbital Ray is placed in front of the team during a fight, so allies move through it.\n\n## Kiriko · `kiriko`\n- Healing Ofuda goes to allies taking damage.\n- Kunai is thrown at heads while the team is healthy.\n- Swift Step is used to escape to an ally away from danger, or to reach an ally in trouble.\n- Protection Suzu is held for big threats (enemy ultimates, anti-heal, sleep, burst on an ally), not spent on small damage.\n- Kitsune Rush is used as the team engages, along a path the team follows.\n\n## Lifeweaver · `lifeweaver`\n- Healing Blossom is charged before it is released on an ally taking damage.\n- Thorn Volley damages enemies while allies are healthy.\n- Life Grip saves an ally who is low or about to be hit by an ultimate, not pulling allies out of good positions.\n- Petal Platform lifts allies to high ground or blocks an enemy path.\n- Rejuvenating Dash is used to dodge and to stay out of enemy reach.\n- Tree of Life is placed against burst or an enemy ultimate, where the team is fighting.\n\n## Lúcio · `lucio`\n- Crossfade is on Speed Boost to engage or retreat and on Healing Boost while the team takes damage.\n- Amp It Up is timed with the engage (speed) or with burst damage on the team (healing).\n- Soundwave knocks enemies off ledges, off the objective or away from allies.\n- Wall Ride keeps him moving and hard to hit while he stays in range of his allies.\n- Sound Barrier is used against an enemy ultimate or burst, with allies in range.\n- Sonic Amplifier shots are aimed at heads at close range.\n\n## Mauga · `mauga`\n- His chainguns are fired at targets in range: Incendiary Chaingun sets them on fire, and critical hits give Berserker's temporary health.\n- Overrun is used to engage or to escape (he is unstoppable while charging), with the stomp aimed at enemies.\n- Cardiac Overdrive is used in fights where he and his allies deal damage, so they heal through it.\n- Cage Fight traps enemies inside with him and his team, cutting them off from their backline.\n- He stays close enough for his guns and keeps firing instead of stopping between targets.\n\n## Mei · `mei`\n- Endothermic Blaster's spray is used at close range; icicles are aimed at heads at range.\n- Ice Wall splits the enemy team, blocks a sightline, saves an ally or closes a choke.\n- Cryo-Freeze is used to avoid dying or to wait out an enemy ultimate.\n- Blizzard is placed where enemies can't easily get out (the objective, a choke), with the team following up.\n- She fights at close to medium range next to cover.\n\n## Mercy · `mercy`\n- Caduceus Staff heals the ally taking damage and boosts the damage of allies who are shooting.\n- Guardian Angel is used to move between allies and dodge, with the jump and crouch launches.\n- Resurrect is used from cover or once enemies look away, not in front of the enemy team.\n- Valkyrie is used to keep the team alive through a fight or to turn a fight.\n- Angelic Descent is used to fall slowly and be harder to hit.\n- She stays behind cover between her allies, not in the open.\n\n## Mizuki · `mizuki`\n- Healing Kasa is thrown where allies stand close together so it bounces between them.\n- Spirit Glaive damage is woven in between heals, which also strengthens Remedy Aura.\n- Binding Chain is used on divers or flankers threatening the backline, not on a tank in front.\n- Katashiro Return is kept as an escape: leap out and teleport back, or leap away from a dive.\n- Kekkai Sanctuary is placed where the team fights so it heals and absorbs enemy projectiles.\n- She stays within Remedy Aura range of allies instead of drifting off alone.\n\n## Moira · `moira`\n- Biotic Grasp heals allies taking damage; its damage beam refills biotic energy between heals.\n- Biotic Orb heals when several allies are hurt, and damages enemies in tight spaces or groups.\n- Fade is used to escape or to dodge abilities.\n- Coalescence is used to win a fight by healing several allies and damaging several enemies.\n- She stays close enough to her team to heal them.\n\n## Orisa · `orisa`\n- Augmented Fusion Driver is fired without overheating in the middle of a fight.\n- Energy Javelin interrupts an enemy ability or ultimate, or knocks a target into a wall.\n- Fortify is used against crowd control, burst damage or enemy ultimates.\n- Javelin Spin is used to block projectiles, push enemies or move forward quickly.\n- Terra Surge pulls enemies together and is unleashed while they are grouped.\n- Her cooldowns are spread out, not all used at once.\n\n## Pharah · `pharah`\n- Rocket Launcher rockets hit targets directly, or hit the ground under grouped enemies.\n- Jump Jet and Jet Dash are used to reach angles and to dodge, with fuel kept so she doesn't drop.\n- Concussive Blast knocks enemies off ledges or away from her, or is used to move.\n- Barrage is used from cover or height on grouped or immobile enemies, not in front of hitscan heroes.\n- She stays near cover, out of enemy hitscan sightlines.\n\n## Ramattra · `ramattra`\n- In Omnic Form, Void Accelerator pokes from range and Void Barrier blocks damage for the team.\n- Nemesis Form is used when enemies are in reach of Pummel, not at long range.\n- Ravenous Vortex pulls down flying or mobile enemies and slows them.\n- Annihilation is used as the team engages, and he stays in contact with enemies so it lasts longer.\n- He switches to Nemesis Form for brawls and back to Omnic Form to poke and protect.\n\n## Reaper · `reaper`\n- Hellfire Shotguns are fired at close range, aimed at heads.\n- Shadow Step is used to flank or take an off-angle out of sight.\n- Wraith Form is used to escape or to dodge an ability.\n- Death Blossom is used when grouped enemies are close and can't escape.\n- He engages from close cover, so The Reaping heals him as he deals damage.\n\n## Reinhardt · `reinhardt`\n- Barrier Field is held against heavy damage to protect allies, and lowered to attack.\n- Rocket Hammer swings land on targets in reach.\n- Fire Strike is thrown at grouped enemies for damage and ultimate charge.\n- Charge is used to pin a target with a clear path and the team nearby, not into the enemy team alone.\n- Earthshatter hits enemies who can't avoid it, with the team ready to follow up.\n- He manages Barrier Field's health so it doesn't break in the middle of a fight.\n\n## Roadhog · `roadhog`\n- Scrap Gun is fired at close range.\n- Chain Hook pulls squishy targets, followed by Scrap Gun shots to finish them.\n- Take a Breather is used to survive burst, near cover.\n- Trash Compactor absorbs enemy projectiles and the scrap ball is thrown back at enemies.\n- Whole Hog knocks enemies off the objective, off ledges or away from his allies.\n\n## Shion · `shion`\n- Kira Pistols are fired at targets in range; Execution is held to tighten it at range and released wide up close.\n- Joyride is used to flank or to escape, and the bike is launched into enemies.\n- Evade is used to dodge damage, and the overhealth is used to win a duel.\n- Satsuriku Spree is used on low or grouped enemies with the team ready.\n- He flanks targets out of position, not the whole enemy team.\n\n## Sierra · `sierra`\n- Tracking Shot lands on a target before sustained Helix Rifle fire, so the tracking shots pay off.\n- Helix Rifle is fired in sustained bursts at range, because the spiral gains accuracy with sustained fire.\n- Anchor Drone is placed before a fight and its grapple used to reach high ground or as the escape, not wasted mid-duel.\n- Tremor Charge is thrown into grouped enemies or to finish a target, not into empty space.\n- Trailblazer's explosives are aimed along the enemy's path or position, not where nobody stands.\n- The perk choice fits the match (Medi-Drone for sustain, Locked In for duels) when the perk screen is visible.\n\n## Sigma · `sigma`\n- Experimental Barrier blocks damage for the team and is recalled before it breaks.\n- Kinetic Grasp absorbs projectiles and enemy ultimates.\n- Accretion knocks down a diver or interrupts an enemy ultimate.\n- Hyperspheres are fired at grouped enemies or around corners.\n- Gravitic Flux lifts several enemies, with the team ready to follow up.\n\n## Sojourn · `sojourn`\n- Railgun's primary fire builds energy before railgun shots; no low-energy rails into tanks.\n- Railgun shots are aimed at heads at range.\n- Power Slide and the slide-jump are used to reach angles or escape, not to walk into the enemy team.\n- Disruptor Shot is placed to zone enemies or hold them in place for the team's damage.\n- Overclock is used when targets are in sight and the team can follow up.\n\n## Soldier: 76 · `soldier-76`\n- Heavy Pulse Rifle is fired in short bursts at long range, not held down.\n- Helix Rockets are combined with primary fire to finish targets.\n- Biotic Field (or Stim Pack, with that perk) is used during duels behind cover, not in the open.\n- Sprint is used for rotations and to reach high ground, then held as an escape.\n- Tactical Visor is used when several enemies are in sight, not on one tank.\n\n## Sombra · `sombra`\n- Hotfix goes to allies taking damage, and is used to hack health packs and enemy deployables.\n- Cyberspace is fired where allies fight and enemies stand, so it weakens enemies and heals allies.\n- Translocator is thrown to a safe spot before she engages, and used to escape.\n- EMP is used when several enemies are near her, with the team ready to follow up.\n- Machine Pistol damages enemies at close range while allies are healthy.\n\n## Symmetra · `symmetra`\n- Photon Projector's beam stays on targets at close range; charged orbs are fired at grouped enemies at range.\n- Sentry Turrets are placed in unexpected spots that cover a choke or a flank route.\n- Teleporter brings the team to an angle or shortens the walk back from spawn.\n- Photon Barrier is placed to block enemy damage or an enemy ultimate during a fight.\n- She fights at close range only with her turrets nearby.\n\n## Torbjörn · `torbjorn`\n- Rivet Gun's primary fire is aimed at heads at range; its short-range fire is used up close.\n- Deploy Turret is placed where it covers the objective or a flank and doesn't die at once.\n- Forge Hammer repairs the turret while it is safe to do so.\n- Overload is used in duels and when enemies dive him.\n- Molten Core is placed on tanks or on a choke the enemy has to walk through.\n\n## Tracer · `tracer`\n- Pulse Pistols are fired at close range, with reloads done out of sight.\n- Blink is used to dodge and to close the distance, with a charge kept to escape.\n- Recall is used to escape after taking damage, before she is low enough to die.\n- Pulse Bomb is stuck to a target the team can kill, or onto grouped enemies.\n- She attacks the backline from flank angles, not from the front.\n\n## Vendetta · `vendetta`\n- Palatine Fang's combo is finished so the overhead slash lands on a target.\n- Warding Stance blocks frontal damage and deflects melee attacks, and is released before its energy runs out.\n- Projected Edge is fired from Warding Stance at enemies out of sword range.\n- Whirlwind Dash and Soaring Slice close the distance on isolated targets, with one kept to escape.\n- Sundering Blade is used on grouped enemies or enemies behind defenses, since it cleaves through most of them.\n\n## Venture · `venture`\n- SMART Excavator charges are aimed at targets at close range.\n- Drill Dash is used to engage or to escape, faster while burrowed.\n- Burrow is used to approach unseen or to dodge damage, emerging on top of enemies.\n- Tectonic Shock is used when several enemies are on the ground in front of her.\n- She engages isolated targets and leaves while she still has a way out.\n\n## Widowmaker · `widowmaker`\n- Scoped Widow's Kiss shots are charged and aimed at heads.\n- Grappling Hook is used to reach high ground and to escape divers.\n- Venom Mine is placed on a flank route behind her.\n- Infra-Sight is used before the team engages, to show where enemies are.\n- She changes position after a kill or once she is spotted.\n\n## Winston · `winston`\n- Tesla Cannon hits several enemies at once, and charged shots finish targets out of the cone.\n- Jump Pack dives the backline together with the team, and is kept or used to get out.\n- Barrier Projector is placed to block the enemy team's damage during the dive.\n- Primal Rage is used to knock enemies off ledges, to survive, or to finish targets.\n- He dives isolated targets and leaves once his cooldowns are used.\n\n## Wrecking Ball · `wrecking-ball`\n- Grappling Claw builds speed to hit grouped enemies.\n- Piledriver lands on grouped enemies, followed by Quad Cannons fire.\n- Adaptive Shield is used close to several enemies, so it gives more extra health.\n- Minefield is placed on a choke or the objective the enemy needs.\n- Quad Cannons are fired at targets in range between engages.\n- He leaves to pick up health packs when he is low, instead of staying in.\n\n## Wuyang · `wuyang`\n- Restorative Stream stays on the ally taking damage, with manual healing when they're in trouble.\n- Xuanwu Staff orbs are guided onto enemies, with empowered explosions on grouped enemies.\n- Rushing Torrent is used to reposition or to escape.\n- Tidal Blast is placed on an ally (or himself) under focus, while enemies are close enough to be knocked down.\n- Guardian Wave is sent through the team when enemies push, knocking them back.\n\n## Zarya · `zarya`\n- Particle Barrier and Projected Barrier absorb damage to build energy; Projected Barrier saves an ally under focus or crowd control.\n- Particle Cannon's beam is used at close range, especially at high energy.\n- Energy grenades are fired at range or at grouped enemies.\n- Graviton Surge pulls several enemies together, with the team ready to follow up.\n- Barriers aren't used while nobody is shooting.\n\n## Zenyatta · `zenyatta`\n- Orb of Discord is on the target the team focuses.\n- Orb of Harmony stays on the ally taking damage.\n- Orb of Destruction volleys are charged and aimed at heads.\n- Transcendence is used against an enemy ultimate or burst on the team.\n- Snap Kick knocks divers away from him.\n- He stays behind cover, out of divers' reach.\n";
